  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nOn websites that don't provide a favicon, the browser automatically attempts to access `/favicon.ico`, resulting in unnecessary network traffic and 404 responses.\n\nA workaround for this issue is to use a data scheme. e.g. `<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\">`\n\nHowever, I think it would be better if there were a standardized method defined in the HTML specification.\n\nFor example...\n\n```html\n<link rel=\"icon\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" type=\"none\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" other-attribute=\"...\">\n```\n",
